"Decode this ciphertext — it's a Caesar cipher."
CTF problems (picoCTF, OverTheWire, CryptoPals challenges) almost always hide the shift.
Puzzle books, escape rooms, or geocaching often give just the ciphertext.
Homework that says "crack this message" or "find the hidden text".

Why hide it? To teach:
Brute force (try all 25 shifts — trivial on computer, doable by hand for short text).
Frequency analysis (E is most common → find which ciphertext letter maps to it).
Letter patterns (common words like "the", "and", single-letter "a"/"i", doubles like "ll").
English recognition (one decryption will suddenly make sense).



